description.text:
The student who completes the undergraduate course with an achievement coefficient equal to or greater than 8.5 (eight point five) in the subjects of the curriculum is awarded the Academic Laureate, provided that all the following requirements are met:
• no final grade lower than 8.0 (eight);
• at least 2/3 (two thirds) of final grades equal to or greater than 9.0 (nine);
• at least 50% of the course taken at PUCRS, without any penalty provided for in the disciplinary regime.
The fulfillment of the requirements established in this article is verified by the Academic Collegiate of the School and by the Dean of Graduation and Continuing Education, in what is within their competence.
